+
+## Help Themes
+
+A {class}`HelpTheme` styles parts of the help page with {func}`style`: the section headings, the option, argument and
+command names in the first column, the `Usage:` prefix, and the bracket at the end of an option's help line. Set it with
+the `help_theme` context setting; subcommands inherit it from their group.
+
+```python
+THEME = click.HelpTheme(
+    heading={"fg": "yellow", "bold": True},
+    option={"fg": "cyan"},
+    usage={"bold": True},
+    extra={"dim": True},
+)
+
+@click.group(context_settings={"help_theme": THEME})
+def cli():
+    pass
+```
+
+Each field takes the keyword arguments of {func}`style`, or `None` to leave that part plain. Styles take no columns, so
+the page is laid out exactly as without a theme. As with any styled output, the codes are removed when the help is not
+written to a terminal, unless colors are forced with `color=True`. A custom {class}`HelpFormatter` gets the theme as its
+`theme` argument and as {attr}`HelpFormatter.theme`, and {meth}`HelpTheme.apply` styles a text as one of the parts.
